WEBVTT

1
00:01:18.623 --> 00:01:20.759
How do you feel?

2
00:01:20.793 --> 00:01:22.895
Alive.

3
00:01:22.929 --> 00:01:24.397
What do you see?

4
00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.766
White... Room...

5
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:30.602
Chair...

6
00:01:31.870 --> 00:01:33.740
Carlo Bugatti throne chair...

7
00:01:34.673 --> 00:01:36.676
Piano...

8
00:01:36.709 --> 00:01:38.578
Steinway.
concert grand.

9
00:01:40.412 --> 00:01:41.414
Art...

10
00:01:42.448 --> 00:01:46.651
<i>The Nativity
by Piero della Francesca.</i>

11
00:01:48.486 --> 00:01:50.289
I am your father.

12
00:01:53.826 --> 00:01:55.161
Ambulate.

13
00:02:00.498 --> 00:02:01.600
Perfect.

14
00:02:05.471 --> 00:02:06.838
Am I?

15
00:02:06.872 --> 00:02:08.074
Perfect?

16
00:02:08.908 --> 00:02:10.976
Your son?

17
00:02:11.009 --> 00:02:12.778
You are my creation.

18
00:02:15.747 --> 00:02:17.249
What is your name?

19
00:02:28.894 --> 00:02:30.962
David.

20
00:02:30.997 --> 00:02:32.331
Why don't you play something?

21
00:02:44.543 --> 00:02:47.346
What would you like me
to play?

22
00:02:47.378 --> 00:02:48.480
Wagner.

23
00:02:49.147 --> 00:02:50.383
Selection?

24
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:52.718
Dealer's choice.

25
00:03:10.201 --> 00:03:12.805
<i>The Entry of the Gods
into Valhalla...</i>

26
00:03:14.272 --> 00:03:16.609
A little anemic
without the orchestra.

27
00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:28.121
May I ask you
a question. Father?

28
00:03:29.721 --> 00:03:30.789
Please.

29
00:03:31.356 --> 00:03:33.258
If you created me...

30
00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.128
who created you?

31
00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:42.467
The question of the ages...

32
00:03:42.501 --> 00:03:45.538
which I hope you and I
will answer one day.

33
00:03:46.070 --> 00:03:47.372
All this.

34
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:50.476
All these wonders of art...

35
00:03:50.509 --> 00:03:53.312
design.
human ingenuity...

36
00:03:54.278 --> 00:03:55.713
all utterly meaningless

37
00:03:55.747 --> 00:03:58.551
in the face of the only
question that matters.

38
00:04:00.885 --> 00:04:02.754
Where do we come from?

39
00:04:05.691 --> 00:04:07.225
I refuse to believe...

40
00:04:07.259 --> 00:04:10.029
that mankind
is a random byproduct

41
00:04:10.062 --> 00:04:11.597
of molecular circumstance...

42
00:04:13.265 --> 00:04:17.836
no more than the result of
mere biological chance.

43
00:04:17.870 --> 00:04:19.204
No.

44
00:04:19.237 --> 00:04:21.741
There must be more.

45
00:04:21.773 --> 00:04:23.875
And you and I. son...

46
00:04:24.776 --> 00:04:26.344
we will find it.

47
00:04:28.514 --> 00:04:32.417
Allow me. then.
a moment to consider.

48
00:04:32.451 --> 00:04:36.455
You seek your creator.
I am looking at mine.

49
00:04:37.723 --> 00:04:40.927
I will serve you.
Yet. you are human.

50
00:04:42.326 --> 00:04:45.497
You will die.
I will not.

51
00:04:52.538 --> 00:04:54.473
Bring me this tea. David.

52
00:04:56.874 --> 00:04:58.310
Bring me the tea.

53
00:06:30.269 --> 00:06:31.435
<i>Walter.</i>

54
00:06:31.470 --> 00:06:33.906
<i>it's time to recharge
the energy grid.</i>

55
00:06:33.939 --> 00:06:35.674
<i>Please report to the bridge.</i>

56
00:06:35.706 --> 00:06:37.509
On my way. Mother.

57
00:06:43.115 --> 00:06:45.484
Deploying energy
recharge sails now.

58
00:07:12.377 --> 00:07:16.115
<i>Sails deployed.
Recharge commencing now.</i>

59
00:07:34.766 --> 00:07:37.435
<i>Seven bells and all's well.</i>

60
00:07:43.475 --> 00:07:46.112
<i>Crew checks complete.</i>

61
00:07:48.879 --> 00:07:53.418
Use security code
31564-F.

62
00:08:31.323 --> 00:08:34.425
<i>Walter.
we have a problem.</i>

63
00:08:34.459 --> 00:08:38.430
<i>A neutrino burst was
detected in Sector 106.</i>

64
00:08:38.463 --> 00:08:41.534
<i>This could trigger
a destructive event.</i>

65
00:08:41.566 --> 00:08:44.101
<i>Report to the bridge.
immediately.</i>

66
00:08:44.135 --> 00:08:46.205
On my way. Mother.

67
00:08:51.542 --> 00:08:53.645
<i>Warning.
Power surge detected.</i>

68
00:08:53.679 --> 00:08:56.415
Mother. retract
the energy sails.

69
00:08:56.448 --> 00:08:57.582
And channel all...

70
00:08:57.616 --> 00:08:59.151
reserve power.

71
00:09:03.155 --> 00:09:04.656
<i>Emergency.</i>

72
00:09:04.689 --> 00:09:07.258
<i>Threat level critical.</i>

73
00:09:07.292 --> 00:09:09.627
Initiate emergency
crew revival.

74
00:09:12.598 --> 00:09:13.732
<i>Attention.</i>

75
00:09:13.766 --> 00:09:15.800
<i>Non-essential personnel.</i>

76
00:09:15.834 --> 00:09:19.436
<i>evacuate the cryo-chamber
immediately.</i>

77
00:09:19.470 --> 00:09:21.072
Daniels!
Look at me. look at me.

78
00:09:21.106 --> 00:09:23.540
I need you to get up. okay?
We're coming out early.

79
00:09:23.574 --> 00:09:25.410
Override the SSP...

80
00:09:25.443 --> 00:09:26.712
and breach
the chamber now.

81
00:09:26.744 --> 00:09:28.779
<i>Warning.
Threat level critical.</i>

82
00:09:28.814 --> 00:09:29.848
It's okay.

83
00:09:30.582 --> 00:09:32.918
Hey. Come on up.
Come on.

84
00:09:47.598 --> 00:09:49.334
Captain!
Captain!

85
00:09:49.367 --> 00:09:51.936
Jacob! Wake up!

86
00:09:51.970 --> 00:09:52.870
Let them work.

87
00:09:52.904 --> 00:09:54.473
Jake!
My God!

88
00:09:54.506 --> 00:09:56.374
-Daniels. come on!
-Jake!

89
00:09:56.407 --> 00:09:57.908
Let them work.

90
00:09:57.943 --> 00:09:58.977
Let them work!

91
00:10:01.612 --> 00:10:02.982
-Get it open!
-Come on!

92
00:10:08.353 --> 00:10:10.222
Jake! Jake!

93
00:10:10.988 --> 00:10:12.290
No!

94
00:10:12.324 --> 00:10:14.324
Get her out of there!
Get her back!

95
00:10:17.295 --> 00:10:18.564
Stay back!

96
00:12:11.876 --> 00:12:15.146
<i>Hey! Where are you?
I miss you.</i>

97
00:12:15.946 --> 00:12:17.782
<i>Would you take
a look at this?</i>

98
00:12:17.815 --> 00:12:19.050
<i>I know. I know.</i>

99
00:12:19.084 --> 00:12:20.685
<i>I said I wouldn't go
without you...</i>

100
00:12:22.454 --> 00:12:23.588
<i>-You all right?
-Yeah.</i>

101
00:12:24.823 --> 00:12:26.925
<i>Look at this!</i>

102
00:12:26.959 --> 00:12:28.560
<i>Now get your ass up here.</i>

103
00:12:28.593 --> 00:12:31.295
<i>I can't make any promises.</i>

104
00:12:31.329 --> 00:12:32.830
<i>I love you.</i>

105
00:12:46.243 --> 00:12:48.178
They're your crew now.

106
00:12:48.213 --> 00:12:49.747
They need a leader.

107
00:12:49.781 --> 00:12:51.849
I know.

108
00:12:51.882 --> 00:12:53.285
You believe in me.
right?

109
00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.776
Sorry I'm late. sir.

110
00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:20.211
No. it's okay.

111
00:13:24.181 --> 00:13:26.117
I can't think of any
other way to say it

112
00:13:26.151 --> 00:13:28.886
than to say it.

113
00:13:28.920 --> 00:13:33.724
We have suffered
a monumental tragedy.

114
00:13:33.757 --> 00:13:36.927
And I'm gonna do
the best that I can to...

115
00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:40.231
live up to Jacob's
fine example

116
00:13:40.265 --> 00:13:42.400
as your captain.

117
00:13:42.434 --> 00:13:47.005
But he will be
sorely missed.

118
00:13:47.039 --> 00:13:49.741
And I'm grateful in advance
for. your support.

119
00:13:49.774 --> 00:13:53.011
So. we lost 47 colonists...

120
00:13:53.045 --> 00:13:57.082
and 16. second-generation
embryos...

121
00:13:57.982 --> 00:14:00.017
and obviously.
one crew member.

122
00:14:00.051 --> 00:14:02.519
The current structural
integrity of the ship

123
00:14:02.554 --> 00:14:04.923
is holding at 83%...

124
00:14:04.955 --> 00:14:07.691
but we have many
secondary systems

125
00:14:07.724 --> 00:14:09.494
that are offline.

126
00:14:09.527 --> 00:14:11.528
So. what was it?

127
00:14:11.563 --> 00:14:12.730
A highly charged shockwave

128
00:14:12.763 --> 00:14:14.699
from a nearby
stellar ignition.

129
00:14:14.733 --> 00:14:16.233
As the sails were
deploying for recharge...

130
00:14:16.267 --> 00:14:18.435
we absorbed the full
brunt of the storm.

131
00:14:18.469 --> 00:14:19.271
Walter...

132
00:14:19.304 --> 00:14:20.572
I will want you and Mother
to undergo

133
00:14:20.604 --> 00:14:22.105
a complete
core code review...

134
00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:24.876
so we can understand how this
happened in the first place.

135
00:14:24.910 --> 00:14:27.178
It was a random
localized event. sir.

136
00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:30.547
There's no way to detect
spontaneous stellar flares...

137
00:14:30.582 --> 00:14:31.784
until it's too late.

138
00:14:32.584 --> 00:14:34.017
It was bad luck.

139
00:14:34.050 --> 00:14:35.554
Faris.
I don't believe in luck.

140
00:14:35.587 --> 00:14:37.021
I'm not interested in luck.

141
00:14:37.055 --> 00:14:39.558
I prefer that we be
more capable...

142
00:14:39.590 --> 00:14:40.624
and prepared than lucky.

143
00:14:40.659 --> 00:14:42.327
Observation. reflection.
faith...

144
00:14:42.359 --> 00:14:43.161
and determination.

145
00:14:43.194 --> 00:14:44.996
In this way.
we may navigate the path

146
00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.031
as it unfolds before us.

147
00:14:47.064 --> 00:14:48.233
All right?
And we have. what?

148
00:14:48.266 --> 00:14:50.868
Eight more
recharge cycles to go...

149
00:14:50.901 --> 00:14:52.304
before we get
to Origae-6?

150
00:14:53.371 --> 00:14:54.239
Is that a question. sir?

151
00:14:54.271 --> 00:14:55.806
Yes. Walter.
that's a question.

152
00:14:55.839 --> 00:14:57.108
That is correct.

153
00:15:00.178 --> 00:15:02.513
So. let's get this ship fixed.
Okay?

154
00:15:02.546 --> 00:15:04.548
Let's.
get to work.

155
00:15:04.583 --> 00:15:06.017
Sir.
excuse me. sir.

156
00:15:06.351 --> 00:15:08.052
Yes.

157
00:15:08.085 --> 00:15:12.122
We just lost 47 colonists
and our captain.

158
00:15:12.156 --> 00:15:13.324
We need to
acknowledge that.

159
00:15:13.358 --> 00:15:15.359
Sergeant Lope.
I completely understand.

160
00:15:15.392 --> 00:15:17.995
But if we don't make
these repairs...

161
00:15:18.029 --> 00:15:21.500
we will lose
all the colonists.

162
00:15:21.532 --> 00:15:23.668
But we should do something
for Captain Branson. at least.

163
00:15:23.702 --> 00:15:25.537
This is not a
discussion. Tennessee.

164
00:15:31.642 --> 00:15:32.844
Hey.

165
00:15:33.878 --> 00:15:35.245
The terraforming module
is stable...

166
00:15:35.279 --> 00:15:37.015
but the connecting strut
took some damage.

167
00:15:37.047 --> 00:15:39.483
I still need
to check the vehicles.

168
00:15:42.554 --> 00:15:43.555
I can help...

169
00:15:44.521 --> 00:15:46.123
if you like.

170
00:15:46.656 --> 00:15:47.758
Thanks.

171
00:15:47.791 --> 00:15:49.793
Walter.
How long do you predict

172
00:15:49.827 --> 00:15:51.963
before we can
make our next jump?

173
00:15:51.997 --> 00:15:55.567
Repairs should take
approximately 48 hours.

174
00:15:55.599 --> 00:15:58.135
But we should make an effort
to vacate this sector...

175
00:15:58.169 --> 00:15:59.569
in case of after-flares.

176
00:15:59.603 --> 00:16:00.838
Absolutely. I agree.

177
00:16:00.872 --> 00:16:03.007
So let's get to work.
Dismissed. Thank you.

178
00:16:08.747 --> 00:16:10.515
<i>C-62. open.</i>

179
00:16:10.547 --> 00:16:13.951
Seal C-62.
Open airlock 17.

180
00:16:21.593 --> 00:16:23.428
Open door
to Terraforming Bay.

181
00:16:33.104 --> 00:16:34.272
Slack.

182
00:16:35.839 --> 00:16:38.075
Tension is at 15% down.

183
00:16:40.645 --> 00:16:41.980
Arming.

184
00:16:47.818 --> 00:16:48.920
Secure.

185
00:16:48.954 --> 00:16:50.388
Copy that.

186
00:17:02.866 --> 00:17:04.402
It wasn't my idea.

187
00:17:07.738 --> 00:17:09.607
Jake had this dream
of us building

188
00:17:09.641 --> 00:17:11.575
a cabin on a new world.

189
00:17:14.545 --> 00:17:16.381
Like pioneers.

190
00:17:18.449 --> 00:17:19.951
Cabin on a lake.

191
00:17:23.220 --> 00:17:25.356
There's a lake
in the terraforming zone

192
00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:27.257
on Origae-6.

193
00:17:27.292 --> 00:17:30.362
I mean. a real cabin
made of real wood.

194
00:17:32.096 --> 00:17:34.064
So. in the ship's stores
there's enough wood

195
00:17:34.097 --> 00:17:36.167
to build a cabin.

196
00:17:38.003 --> 00:17:40.438
Axes and saws
and metal nails...

197
00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:43.407
which I don't have a clue
what to do with.

198
00:17:47.813 --> 00:17:49.214
All of this...

199
00:17:50.681 --> 00:17:52.217
to start our new life.

200
00:17:54.686 --> 00:17:57.022
Now I wonder. why bother?

201
00:17:59.224 --> 00:18:03.495
Because you promised to build
a log cabin on a lake.

202
00:18:13.505 --> 00:18:15.273
<i>This was his favorite.</i>

203
00:18:15.305 --> 00:18:17.941
<i>A man of taste.</i>

204
00:18:17.976 --> 00:18:19.343
<i>Straight up.</i>

205
00:18:19.376 --> 00:18:22.479
<i>No ice. no water.
no chaser...</i>

206
00:18:22.514 --> 00:18:24.449
No shit.

207
00:18:28.952 --> 00:18:30.354
Walter?

208
00:18:30.389 --> 00:18:31.456
When in Rome.

209
00:18:34.124 --> 00:18:35.526
<i>To all the good people.</i>

210
00:18:35.559 --> 00:18:36.594
<i>gone too soon.</i>

211
00:18:37.228 --> 00:18:39.564
May we remember them.

212
00:18:39.597 --> 00:18:41.432
Remember them.

213
00:19:21.773 --> 00:19:23.742
Chris.

214
00:19:25.776 --> 00:19:28.246
They disobeyed
a direct order.

215
00:19:29.714 --> 00:19:31.282
She buried her husband.

216
00:19:31.314 --> 00:19:33.818
No. Karine. that's not it.
They don't trust me.

217
00:19:33.852 --> 00:19:35.018
And they don't
for the same reason

218
00:19:35.052 --> 00:19:36.154
the company
didn't trust me...

219
00:19:36.187 --> 00:19:37.289
to lead this mission.

220
00:19:37.322 --> 00:19:39.290
Because you can't be
a person of faith...

221
00:19:39.323 --> 00:19:40.992
and be counted on
to make qualified.

222
00:19:41.026 --> 00:19:42.660
rational decisions.

223
00:19:42.692 --> 00:19:46.296
You're an extremist. you know.
You're a lunatic.

224
00:19:46.331 --> 00:19:49.401
When we get
to where we're going...

225
00:19:49.433 --> 00:19:51.168
these people won't be
your crew anymore.

226
00:19:51.201 --> 00:19:53.438
They will be
your neighbors.

227
00:19:53.471 --> 00:19:54.805
Remember that.

228
00:19:56.007 --> 00:19:58.410
Tread softly. okay?

229
00:20:06.484 --> 00:20:08.019
Faris.
can you hear me?

230
00:20:08.053 --> 00:20:09.187
<i>Copy.</i>

231
00:20:09.219 --> 00:20:10.689
Let's do it.

232
00:20:13.257 --> 00:20:15.860
Damn. y'all should
see this view.

233
00:20:15.893 --> 00:20:17.094
<i>We can't
see anything</i>

234
00:20:17.128 --> 00:20:19.063
<i>until you get
the camera array fixed.</i>

235
00:20:19.096 --> 00:20:21.598
Why don't you look out
the damn window. hon?

236
00:20:21.632 --> 00:20:23.301
<i>Ankor. come on. let's get
this power back on...</i>

237
00:20:23.334 --> 00:20:26.670
<i>so these people can enjoy
the beautiful view.</i>

238
00:20:27.238 --> 00:20:28.606
Almost there.

239
00:20:29.940 --> 00:20:31.042
<i>All right. Ankor.</i>

240
00:20:31.074 --> 00:20:32.242
<i>let me know when
you're in position...</i>

241
00:20:32.276 --> 00:20:34.645
<i>and we can get
this party started.</i>

242
00:20:34.679 --> 00:20:36.514
I'm in position.

243
00:21:05.809 --> 00:21:07.211
Contact.

244
00:21:15.719 --> 00:21:17.354
<i>All good. Tee?</i>

245
00:21:17.388 --> 00:21:19.791
All right. We're clear.

246
00:21:19.824 --> 00:21:21.159
<i>Reel her in.</i>

247
00:21:21.191 --> 00:21:23.059
All right.

248
00:21:23.093 --> 00:21:25.663
Winch engaging. Tee.

249
00:21:27.699 --> 00:21:29.534
Reeling her in.

250
00:21:32.469 --> 00:21:34.506
<i>Working like a dream.</i>

251
00:21:48.919 --> 00:21:50.088
<i>There we go.</i>

252
00:21:50.121 --> 00:21:51.222
<i>And we're back up.</i>

253
00:21:51.255 --> 00:21:52.690
Well done. Tee.

254
00:21:52.724 --> 00:21:54.058
We are live down here.

255
00:21:54.092 --> 00:21:55.193
Come on in.

256
00:21:55.226 --> 00:21:56.727
<i>Don't leave
without me now.</i>

257
00:21:56.760 --> 00:21:59.396
Permission to leave
without him. sir?

258
00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:00.798
Welcome back. Danny.

259
00:22:01.699 --> 00:22:03.066
Thanks.

260
00:22:03.100 --> 00:22:05.169
All right.
that's me done. Tee.

261
00:22:05.202 --> 00:22:06.804
All right.
I'm following you in.

262
00:22:06.836 --> 00:22:09.574
Please have a cold beer ready
for the weary traveler.

263
00:22:09.606 --> 00:22:10.841
<i>You got it. darlin'.</i>

264
00:22:10.874 --> 00:22:13.178
<i>I will join you
for a cold one.</i>

265
00:22:13.210 --> 00:22:15.012
Faris? Put the...

